{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/73890-legibility-of-the-pod-core-book","id":73890,"title":"Legibility of the PoD core book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-17T14:37:29-08:00","id":73890,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon1.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Legibility of the PoD core book","content":"Has anyone else ordered their copy of Promethean as print on demand? Supplements I don't mind as a PDF but core books I like to have in a format that is compatible with laying on the porch swing on a sunny day. However, while on the whole the quality of my PoD Promethean book was excellent (as was my Second Sight book) I found that the side bars were harder to read as well as pages with a dark background than the original mass production print book that my friend has or the PDF. I believe it has to do with the colors and fonts used. The font in the boxes is italics and thus does not shrink well when made to fit in an 8 1/2 by 11 area even though its a very modest rescaling. Its also slightly gray in the original book which makes it that much harder to read against a gray background. Has anyone else had this issue with their book or did I just catch them on a day where the ink tanks were running low? I tried customer service but they never actually emailed me back, probably because I said it wasn't a problem I felt warranted a return, just something I wanted to bring to their attention if it was fixable for future print runs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T12:34:18-08:00","id":84783,"title":"","content":"I <i>THINK</i> it has to do with the fact that <b>Promethean: the Created</b> PoD is only available as black-and-white rather than full colour. The original book was in colour, albeit very MUTED colours at that. I've found similar things occurred to me with other World of Darkness books (thinking of <i>Goblin Markets</i> for <b>Changeling: the Lost</b>) that were printed b&amp;w from digital sources that contained colour.<br /> <br /> <b>Note</b>: I tried to post this response a few times in the past weeks, but I've been... well, let's just say feeble, okay? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}